[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Machines and Reactors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IF-020
TITLE: State node and Machine surface
STATEMENT: >>>
A State node descriptor carries parent and initial-child links, a Message
handler, and enter and leave hooks. The Machine owns the current node and
application context, but not descriptor storage.

.. code-block:: c

   typedef struct ZStateNode ZStateNode;

   struct ZStateNode {
       ZStateNode const *parent;
       ZStateNode const *initial;
       ZStateHandler handle;
       ZStateHook enter;
       ZStateHook leave;
   };

   void z_machine_init(ZMachine *machine,
                       ZStateNode const *root,
                       void *context);
   void z_machine_start(ZMachine *machine);
   void z_machine_dispatch(ZMachine *machine,
                           ZMsgHandle const *message);
   ZStateNode const *z_machine_state(ZMachine const *machine);

Initialization validates the root and State graph in assertion-enabled builds;
an invalid graph invokes the panic handler with ``Z_PANIC_STATE`` before
initialization completes. In assertion-disabled builds the application is
responsible for supplying a valid graph. Handlers receive a const Message
handle; hooks receive application context. Dispatch performs no allocation.
<<<
